Assistant: I see the issue now. The OptionComponent is meant to be used within a React-Select component, not standalone. Let's modify the preview to properly render it within a Select context.

<file path="apps/web/.temp/dessn-component-routes/OptionComponent-b921da27.tsx">
<change>
<description>Wrap OptionComponent in a Select context to provide necessary styling context</description>
<content>
import React from 'react';
import { useParentState } from '../useIframeState';
import Select, { components } from 'react-select';
import { OptionComponent } from '../../../../packages/ui/components/form/select/components';

export default function ComponentPreview() {
  const [state, setState] = useParentState({
    option: {
      type: "dropdown",
      value: "option1",
      options: ["option1", "option2", "option3"],
      label: "Select Option",
    },
    isMulti: {
      type: "boolean",
      value: false,
      label: "Is Multi Select",
    },
    isSelected: {
      type: "boolean",
      value: false,
      label: "Is Selected",
    },
    needsTeamsUpgrade: {
      type: "boolean",
      value: false,
      label: "Needs Teams Upgrade",
    },
  });

  // Create options array for Select
  const options = state.option.options.map(opt => ({
    label: opt,
    value: opt,
    needsTeamsUpgrade: state.needsTeamsUpgrade.value
  }));

  return (
    <Select
      options={options}
      value={options.find(opt => opt.value === state.option.value)}
      isMulti={state.isMulti.value}
      components={{
        Option: OptionComponent
      }}
      onChange={() => {}}
    />
  );
}
</content>
</change>
</file>

I've made the following changes to fix the error:

1. Imported the full `Select` component from 'react-select'
2. Created a proper options array with the required structure
3. Wrapped the OptionComponent in a Select component context by using it in the components prop
4. Added necessary props to the Select component (options, value, onChange)

This should resolve the "getStyles is not a function" error because now the OptionComponent is receiving the proper context and styling functions it needs from the parent Select component.

The OptionComponent will now have access to all the necessary internal React-Select context, including the styling functions it needs to render properly. The preview should now work without the styling error.

